& [AuthorizedFileSet] is exact
  + [new_module] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/platform_preflight_forms.rs
  + [validator_visibility] is one pub(crate) visibility change in crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/topology_forms.rs
  + [module_export] is one module and public vocabulary re-export in crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/lib.rs
  + [governance_files] are source, canonical, exploded, justification, plan, matrix, slice, registry, evidence, solution, proof, review, fault, file-change, turn, map, narrative, and reentry records
  - never: change Cargo.toml or Cargo.lock
  - never: change an existing topology-form validation rule

& [ProfileContract] is exact
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-platform-preflight/0.1
  + [target_triple] is x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
  + [other_profile_or_target] rejects

& [InputRootContract] is lexical
  + [syntax] is extended-DOS uppercase drive absolute path
  + [prefix] is exactly \\?\
  + [drive] is uppercase A through Z followed by colon and backslash
  + [root_form] may end after the drive-root separator
  + [descendant_form] has nonempty backslash-separated components and no trailing separator
  + [maximum_UTF8_bytes] is 32768
  + [forbidden] is relative, drive-relative, ordinary DOS, UNC, volume GUID, device, NT, forward slash, NUL, dot, dot-dot, repeated separator, and trailing descendant separator
  + [existence_check] is absent

& [OutcomeContract] is one closed sum
  + [open_fault] contains only profile, target triple, input root, and nonzero Win32 error
  + [query_fault] contains only profile, target triple, input root, one closed query stage, and nonzero Win32 error
  + [complete] contains profile, target triple, input root, root identity, canonical volume-GUID final path, volume information, remote-protocol information, and disposition
  + [partial_evidence_in_fault] is structurally absent

& [QueryStageContract] is closed
  + [file_id_info] is admitted
  + [final_volume_guid_path] is admitted
  + [volume_information] is admitted
  + [remote_protocol_information] is admitted
  + [other_stage] rejects

& [IdentityContract] reuses proven meaning
  + [root_identity] is StrongFileIdentity with a 64-bit volume serial and exactly 16 identity bytes encoded as 32 lowercase hexadecimal characters
  + [root_volume_guid_path] uses the TopologyReceipt 0.2 canonical volume-GUID grammar
  + [identity_lifetime] is scan-local and not permanent
  + [serial_equivalence] between FileIdInfo u64 and volume-information u32 is not asserted

& [VolumeInformationContract] is complete
  + [volume_name] may be empty, must be NUL-free, and is at most 1024 UTF-8 bytes
  + [volume_serial_number] is an unqualified u32 observation
  + [maximum_component_length] is 1 through 32767
  + [file_system_flags] is raw u32 evidence
  + [file_system_name] is nonblank, NUL-free ASCII of at most 64 bytes

& [RemoteProtocolContract] is bounded
  + [structure_version] is 1 or 2
  + [structure_size] is 116
  + [protocol] is u32
  + [protocol_major_version] is u16
  + [protocol_minor_version] is u16
  + [protocol_revision] is u16
  + [flags] is u32
  + [reserved_fields] are not admitted

& [DispositionContract] is relational
  + [eligible_local_ntfs] requires file_system_name exactly NTFS and protocol zero
  + [reject_remote_protocol] requires protocol nonzero regardless of filesystem name
  + [reject_unsupported_file_system] requires protocol zero and file_system_name other than NTFS
  + [fault_outcomes] have no disposition
  + [protocol_zero] is a policy inference that must be invalidated if target-host evidence or primary documentation contradicts it

& [StrictDecoderContract] is fail closed
  + [unknown_field] rejects
  + [unknown_variant] rejects
  + [semantic_validation] runs after deserialization
  + [NUL] rejects in every text field
  + [error_zero] rejects in every fault
  + [inconsistent_disposition] rejects

& [EffectContract] is zero
  + [Win32_call] is absent
  + [windows_sys_reference] is absent from the new production module
  + [unsafe] is absent
  + [filesystem] is absent
  + [handle] is absent
  + [FFI] is absent
  + [process_environment_clock_random_network_persistence] are absent
  + [fixture_candidate_scanner_receipt] effects are absent
  + [physical_claim] is absent

& [RequirementSet] is M2B-PF-001 through M2B-PF-012
  + [lineage] preserves source, research, exploded meaning, justification, plan, registry, and completed dependency
  + [shape] fixes profile, target, root, outcomes, query stages, evidence products, and dispositions
  + [strictness] fixes bounds, unknown rejection, nonzero faults, completeness, and cross-field validation
  + [effects] fixes a pure supplied-record validator with no observation
  + [closure] requires focused, global, release, lint, docs, audit, evidence, rollback, registry, and support proof

& [Acceptance] is exact
  + [focused] every valid and invalid form class passes in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [static] forbidden effect surfaces are absent from the new module and code delta
  + [Cargo] manifest and lock deltas are zero
  + [global] debug, overflow-checked release, format, lint, build, rustdoc, and audit pass
  + [evidence] every affected evidence manifest is regenerated in dependency order
  + [closure] solution, proof, completion review, readiness, narrative, map, reentry, and publication are current

& [AuthorityBoundary] is pure forms only
  + [allowed] is strict safe-Rust data types, validation, JSON decoding, deterministic tests, visibility-only validator reuse, export, evidence, and proof
  + [forbidden] is Windows API invocation, pointer, buffer, handle, filesystem observation, runtime probe, root eligibility authorization, topology traversal, receipt issuance, fixture, candidate, sandbox, mutation, seal, cleanup, launch, promotion, or physical-readiness claim

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete
  + [source_preserved] is raw source plus immutable manifest
  + [delineated] is pure form, physical preflight, and topology scanner separated
  + [exploded] is twelve requirements, twelve constraints, ten failures, and ten verification gates
  + [semantically_refined] is form, fault, completeness, eligibility, identity, and nonclaim meaning
  + [constraint_checked] is official API meaning, completed ABI probe, existing forms, and effect boundary
  + [pruned] is function calls, handles, pointers, partial evidence, broad targets, recursive topology, and physical claims
  + [data_design_checked] is closed outcome sum, complete products, closed enums, shared identity, and strict decoder
  + [exhaustion_reviewed] is seven_fold_phase_locked
  + [justified] is claim, support, counterargument, invalidation, and rollback
  + [planned] is ordered authority, implementation, verification, evidence, and publication work
  + [registry_recorded] is graph-addressable node, edge, term, and nonedge lineage

